Your Daily & Weekly Workflow

Your idea of a daily directory for analysis is excellent. This creates a quantifiable data stream that you can use to identify trends and improve your focus. Here is a simple, actionable system to put this plan in place:


The Daily Practice: At the start of your workday, create a new directory for that day using the format YYYY-MM-DD. For example, today's folder would be 2025-09-13. Save all files related to your work—code, documents, project notes, even screenshots—into this single folder.

The End-of-Day Review: Before you finish for the day, use the File Organizer app to analyze the directory.

Click Select a Folder to Analyze and choose your daily directory.

Click Deep Analyze on each file.

Click Categorize ✨ on each file to assign it a category.

Click Summarize Day's Work ✨ to get a one-paragraph summary of your day's efforts.

The Weekly Report: At the end of each week, open the app, select the entire week's worth of daily folders, and review the summaries. You'll be able to see at a glance where your time was spent and what you accomplished. This information can help you identify if you're getting sidetracked or if your focus is aligned with your goals.

By turning your digital work into an organized and categorized archive, you're building a system to measure and improve your performance. 
